window.HMO_DATA={"meta":{"title":"Hafez Music Ontology","source":"Ganjoor (ganjoor.net) - public data export github.com/ganjoor/ganjoor-data","sourceCommit":"616e4042699fb2ac9a148b17c7b61221bd3edfe8","count":162,"translated":162},"lexicon":{"مطرب":{"en":"minstrel / musician","cat":"performer"},"طرب":{"en":"mirth, music-making, rapture","cat":"practice"},"بربط":{"en":"barbat (lute)","cat":"instrument"},"پرده":{"en":"mode / fret / tune (lit. veil)","cat":"structure"},"چنگ":{"en":"chang (harp)","cat":"instrument"},"رباب":{"en":"rubab (lute)","cat":"instrument"},"بانگ":{"en":"cry, call, sound","cat":"sound"},"آهنگ":{"en":"melody, tune","cat":"structure"},"صوت":{"en":"sound, voice, chant","cat":"sound"},"ساز":{"en":"instrument, music","cat":"instrument"},"آواز":{"en":"song, voice","cat":"sound"},"نی":{"en":"ney (reed flute)","cat":"instrument"},"رود":{"en":"rud (stringed instrument)","cat":"instrument"},"دف":{"en":"daf (frame drum)","cat":"instrument"},"رقص":{"en":"dance","cat":"practice"},"سماع":{"en":"sama' (mystic audition / dance)","cat":"practice"},"دستان":{"en":"tune, song (dastan)","cat":"structure"},"کمانچه":{"en":"kamancheh (bowed fiddle)","cat":"instrument"},"نغمه":{"en":"melody, song","cat":"structure"},"سرود":{"en":"song, hymn; sang","cat":"sound"}},"counts":{"چنگ":45,"مطرب":42,"رقص":23,"نی":16,"سرود":15,"ساز":15,"بانگ":15,"پرده":14,"سماع":12,"دف":11,"آواز":11,"نغمه":9,"صوت":8,"رباب":7,"بربط":7,"رود":7,"طرب":5,"آهنگ":5,"دستان":2},"lines":[{"id":"ghazal/sh2#3","work":"ghazal","poem":2,"couplet":3,"v":["چه نسبت است به‌ رِندی صَلاح و تقوا را؟","سماعِ وَعظ کجا نغمهٔ رَباب کجا؟"],"w":["رباب","سماع","نغمه"],"hl":[[],[[0,5],[15,20],[21,26]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh2","en":"How could a rogue's way match piety and abstinence?\nWhat has listening to a sermon to do with the song of the rubab?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh3#8","work":"ghazal","poem":3,"couplet":8,"v":["حَدیث از مُطرب و مِی گو و رازِ دَهر کمتر جو","که کس نَگشود و نَگشاید به حکمت این مُعمّا را"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[9,14]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh3","en":"Speak of the minstrel and the wine, and seek less the secret of Time—\nfor no one has solved, or will solve, this riddle by wisdom."},{"id":"ghazal/sh4#8","work":"ghazal","poem":4,"couplet":8,"v":["در آسمان نه عجب گَر به گفتهٔ حافظ","سُرودِ زُهره به رقص آورد مسیحا را"],"w":["سرود","رقص"],"hl":[[],[[0,6],[16,19]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh4","en":"No wonder, in the heavens, if at Hafez's words\nVenus's song should set the Messiah dancing."},{"id":"ghazal/sh11#1","work":"ghazal","poem":11,"couplet":1,"v":["ساقی به نورِ باده برافروز جامِ ما","مطرب بگو که کارِ جهان شُد به کامِ ما"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[],[[0,4]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh11","en":"Cupbearer, light our cup with the glow of wine;\nminstrel, sing: the world's affairs have turned to our desire."},{"id":"ghazal/sh16#8","work":"ghazal","poem":16,"couplet":8,"v":["من از ورع، مِی و مطرب ندیدمی زین پیش","هوای مغبچگانم در این و آن انداخت"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[17,21]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh16","en":"Out of piety, I had never before seen wine or a minstrel—\nmy longing for the tavern boys threw me into this and that."},{"id":"ghazal/sh19#8","work":"ghazal","poem":19,"couplet":8,"v":["ساقی و مُطرب و مِی جمله مُهَیّاست ولی","عیش بی‌یار مُهیّا نشود یار کجاست؟"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[7,12]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh19","en":"Cupbearer, minstrel and wine—all are ready, but\nthere is no joy without the beloved: where is the beloved?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh22#4","work":"ghazal","poem":22,"couplet":4,"v":["دلم ز پرده برون شد، کجایی ای مطرب؟","بنال، هان که از این پرده، کارِ ما به نواست"],"w":["مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[6,10],[29,33]],[[20,24]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh22","en":"My heart has slipped out of the veil—where are you, minstrel?\nSing out! For from this mode our affairs come round to a tune.","note":"Pardeh means a veil and also a fret or mode; the couplet plays on both (“out of the veil”, “from this mode”). Nava means melody, and also ease or provision."},{"id":"ghazal/sh22#9","work":"ghazal","poem":22,"couplet":9,"v":["چه ساز بود که در پرده می‌زد آن مطرب","که رفت عمر و هنوزم دماغ پُر ز هواست"],"w":["ساز","مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[3,6],[17,21],[31,35]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh22","en":"What instrument was it that minstrel played, in his mode, behind the veil—\nthat life has passed, and my head is still full of its tune and longing?","note":"Pardeh means a veil and also a mode: the minstrel plays “in the pardeh”, that is in a mode, or behind the veil. Hava can mean air, longing, or a tune."},{"id":"ghazal/sh29#8","work":"ghazal","poem":29,"couplet":8,"v":["در کُنجِ دِماغم مطلب جای نصیحت","کـ‌این گوشه پر از زمزمهٔ چنگ و رَباب است"],"w":["رباب","چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[25,28],[31,36]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh29","en":"Seek no place for advice in the corner of my mind,\nfor this corner is full of the murmur of harp and rubab."},{"id":"ghazal/sh30#6","work":"ghazal","poem":30,"couplet":6,"v":["مطرب چه پرده ساخت که در پردهٔ سماع","بر اهل وجد و حال، درِ های‌وهو ببست"],"w":["سماع","مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[0,4],[8,12],[24,29],[30,34]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh30","en":"What mode did the minstrel make, that within the mode of the sama'\nhe shut the door of tumult on the people of ecstasy?","note":"Pardeh: veil and mode. The minstrel “makes a pardeh”, i.e. composes in a mode, within the mode of the sama'."},{"id":"ghazal/sh34#3","work":"ghazal","poem":34,"couplet":3,"v":["دلت به وصلِ گل ای بلبلِ صبا خوش باد","که در چمن همه گلبانگِ عاشقانهٔ توست"],"w":["بانگ"],"hl":[[],[[14,21]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh34","en":"May the breeze bring you joy in union with the rose, nightingale,\nfor all through the meadow rings your lover's song."},{"id":"ghazal/sh34#9","work":"ghazal","poem":34,"couplet":9,"v":["سرودِ مجلست اکنون فلک به رقص آرَد","که شعرِ حافظِ شیرین سخن ترانهٔ توست"],"w":["سرود","رقص"],"hl":[[[0,5],[25,28]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh34","en":"The song of your gathering would now set the heavens dancing,\nfor Hafez's sweet-spoken verse is your melody."},{"id":"ghazal/sh35#3","work":"ghazal","poem":35,"couplet":3,"v":["به کام تا نرساند مرا لبش، چون نای","نصیحتِ همه عالم به گوشِ من بادست"],"w":["نی"],"hl":[[[30,33]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh35","en":"Until her lip brings me to my desire, like the reed flute,\nall the world's advice is but wind in my ear."},{"id":"ghazal/sh41#1","work":"ghazal","poem":41,"couplet":1,"v":["اگر چه باده فَرَح بخش و باد گُل‌بیز است","به بانگِ چَنگ مخور مِی که مُحتَسِب تیز است"],"w":["بانگ","چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[3,8],[9,13]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh41","en":"Though wine gives joy and the breeze scatters roses,\ndrink no wine to the sound of the harp—the censor is sharp."},{"id":"ghazal/sh43#3","work":"ghazal","poem":43,"couplet":3,"v":["ناگشوده گُل نِقاب، آهنگِ رحلت ساز کرد","ناله‌ کن بلبل که گلبانگِ دل‌اَفکاران خوش است"],"w":["بانگ"],"hl":[[],[[17,24]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh43","en":"The rose has not yet unveiled, and already she prepares to leave;\nlament, nightingale—the cry of the broken-hearted is sweet."},{"id":"ghazal/sh46#4","work":"ghazal","poem":46,"couplet":4,"v":["گوشم همه بر قولِ نی و نغمهٔ چنگ است","چشمم، همه، بر لعلِ لب و گَردشِ جام است"],"w":["نی","نغمه","چنگ"],"hl":[[[17,19],[22,27],[28,31]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh46","en":"My ear is wholly on the word of the ney and the melody of the harp;\nmy eye wholly on the ruby of her lip and the turning of the cup."},{"id":"ghazal/sh53#2","work":"ghazal","poem":53,"couplet":2,"v":["گَرَم ترانهٔ چنگ صَبوح نیست چه باک","نوایِ من به سَحَر، آهِ عُذْرخواهِ من است"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[13,16]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh53","en":"If I have no song of the morning harp, no matter—\nmy dawn lament is my advocate."},{"id":"ghazal/sh90#8","work":"ghazal","poem":90,"couplet":8,"v":["تا مطربان ز شوقِ مَنَت آگهی دهند","قول و غزل به ساز و نوا می‌فرستمت"],"w":["مطرب","ساز"],"hl":[[[3,9]],[[13,16]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh90","en":"So that the minstrels may tell you of my longing,\nI send you words and verse, with instrument and tune."},{"id":"ghazal/sh90#10","work":"ghazal","poem":90,"couplet":10,"v":["حافظ، سرودِ مجلس ما ذکرِ خیرِ توست","بشتاب هان که اسب و قبا می‌فرستمت"],"w":["سرود"],"hl":[[[6,11]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh90","en":"Hafez, the song of our gathering is praise of you—\nhurry, for I am sending you a horse and a robe of honour."},{"id":"ghazal/sh101#10","work":"ghazal","poem":101,"couplet":10,"v":["قدح مگیر چو حافظ مگر به نالهٔ چنگ","که بسته‌اند بر ابریشمِ طرب دلِ شاد"],"w":["چنگ","طرب"],"hl":[[[30,33]],[[23,26]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh101","en":"Take up no cup, like Hafez, except to the moan of the harp,\nfor the glad heart is bound to the silken strings of mirth.","note":"Abrishum (silk) is also the name for the strings of an instrument such as the harp."},{"id":"ghazal/sh111#9","work":"ghazal","poem":111,"couplet":9,"v":["زیرِ شمشیرِ غمش رقص‌کُنان باید رفت","کـ‌آن که شد کشتهٔ او نیک سرانجام افتاد"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[[16,19]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh111","en":"Beneath the sword of her sorrow we must go dancing,\nfor whoever was slain by her came to a good end."},{"id":"ghazal/sh123#1","work":"ghazal","poem":123,"couplet":1,"v":["مطربِ عشق عجب ساز و نوایی دارد","نقشِ هر نغمه که زد راه به جایی دارد"],"w":["ساز","مطرب","نغمه"],"hl":[[[0,5],[14,17]],[[8,12]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh123","en":"What a marvellous instrument and melody the minstrel of love has—\nevery strain he strikes finds its way somewhere."},{"id":"ghazal/sh123#2","work":"ghazal","poem":123,"couplet":2,"v":["عالَم از نالهٔ عُشّاق مبادا خالی","که خوش‌آهنگ و فرح‌بخش هوایی دارد"],"w":["آهنگ"],"hl":[[],[[7,11]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh123","en":"May the world never be empty of lovers' laments,\nfor it has an air both sweet-toned and joy-giving."},{"id":"ghazal/sh126#5","work":"ghazal","poem":126,"couplet":5,"v":["چنگِ خمیده‌قامت می‌خوانَدَت به عشرت","بشنو که پندِ پیران هیچت زیان ندارد"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[0,4]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh126","en":"The stooped harp is calling you to revelry—\nlisten: an elder's counsel can do you no harm."},{"id":"ghazal/sh133#4","work":"ghazal","poem":133,"couplet":4,"v":["این مُطْرِب اَز کُجاست که سازِ عِراق ساخت؟","وآهَنْگِ بازْگَشْت به راهِ حِجاز کَرْد؟"],"w":["آهنگ","ساز","مطرب"],"hl":[[[4,11],[26,30]],[[0,8]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh133","en":"Where is this minstrel from, who tuned the mode of Iraq,\nthen struck out the tune of return along the road of Hijaz?","note":"Iraq and Hijaz are place names and also names of musical modes (maqam); the couplet uses both senses."},{"id":"ghazal/sh136#5","work":"ghazal","poem":136,"couplet":5,"v":["سروبالایِ من آنگه که درآید به سَماع","چه محل جامهٔ جان را که قبا نتوان کرد؟"],"w":["سماع"],"hl":[[[30,35]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh136","en":"When my cypress-tall beloved enters the sama',\nwhat is the garment of the soul worth, if it cannot be torn like a robe?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh137#5","work":"ghazal","poem":137,"couplet":5,"v":["بدانسان سوخت چون شمعم که بر من","صُراحی گریه و بَربَط فغان کرد"],"w":["بربط"],"hl":[[],[[14,20]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh137","en":"So did I burn like a candle that, over me,\nthe flask wept and the lute lamented."},{"id":"ghazal/sh138#8","work":"ghazal","poem":138,"couplet":8,"v":["مطربا! پرده بگردان و بزن راهِ عراق","که بدین راه بشد یار و ز ما یاد نکرد"],"w":["مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[0,5],[7,11]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh138","en":"Minstrel, change the mode and play the road of Iraq,\nfor by that road my beloved went, and gave me not a thought.","note":"‘Iraq’ is both a country and a musical mode; ‘pardeh bigardan’ is to change mode."},{"id":"ghazal/sh138#9","work":"ghazal","poem":138,"couplet":9,"v":["غزلیاتِ عراقی‌ست سرودِ حافظ","که شنید این رهِ دل‌سوز که فریاد نکرد؟"],"w":["سرود"],"hl":[[[17,22]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh138","en":"The song of Hafez is that of Iraqi's ghazals (and the mode of Iraq):\nwho heard this heart-burning road and did not cry out?","note":"‘Iraqi’ can mean the ghazals of the poet Fakhr al-Din ‘Iraqi, or a song in the mode of Iraq."},{"id":"ghazal/sh142#3","work":"ghazal","poem":142,"couplet":3,"v":["مژدگانی بده ای دل که دگر مطربِ عشق","راهِ مستانه زد و چارهٔ مخموری کرد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[25,30]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh142","en":"Give glad tidings, my heart: once more the minstrel of love\nstruck up a drunken tune and cured our hangover."},{"id":"ghazal/sh142#5","work":"ghazal","poem":142,"couplet":5,"v":["غنچهٔ گُلبُنِ وصلم ز نسیمش بِشِکُفت","مرغ خوشخوان طرب از برگِ گلِ سوری کرد"],"w":["طرب"],"hl":[[],[[12,15]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh142","en":"The bud on the bush of my union opened at her breeze;\nthe sweet-voiced bird rejoiced in song over a petal of the red rose."},{"id":"ghazal/sh144#2","work":"ghazal","poem":144,"couplet":2,"v":["مباش بی می و مُطرب که زیرِ طاقِ سپهر","بدین ترانه غم از دل به در توانی کرد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[13,18]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh144","en":"Do not be without wine and a minstrel: beneath the arch of the sky\nwith such a song you can drive sorrow from the heart."},{"id":"ghazal/sh145#2","work":"ghazal","poem":145,"couplet":2,"v":["چه راه می‌زند این مطربِ مقام شناس","که در میان غزل قول آشنا آورد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[18,23]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh145","en":"What tune does this mode-knowing minstrel strike,\nwho brings a familiar song into the midst of the ghazal?","note":"Maqam-shinas: one who knows the modes. Qawl is a song form, here a familiar song."},{"id":"ghazal/sh145#3","work":"ghazal","poem":145,"couplet":3,"v":["تو نیز باده به چنگ آر و راهِ صحرا گیر","که مرغ نغمه‌سُرا سازِ خوش‌نوا آورد"],"w":["نغمه","ساز"],"hl":[[],[[7,11],[17,21]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh145","en":"You too, take wine in hand and take the road to the meadow,\nfor the singing bird has brought forth a sweet-toned music."},{"id":"ghazal/sh146#5","work":"ghazal","poem":146,"couplet":5,"v":["به قولِ مطرب و ساقی، برون رفتم گَه و بی‌گَه","کز آن راهِ گران، قاصد، خبر، دشوار می‌آورد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[8,12]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh146","en":"At the word of the minstrel and the cupbearer I went out, in season and out—\nfor by that hard road no messenger brings news but with difficulty."},{"id":"ghazal/sh147#2","work":"ghazal","poem":147,"couplet":2,"v":["به مُطربانِ صَبوحی دهیم جامهٔ چاک","بدین نوید که بادِ سحرگهی آورد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[3,11]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh147","en":"To the morning minstrels we shall give our torn robes,\nfor the good news the dawn wind has brought."},{"id":"ghazal/sh153#3","work":"ghazal","poem":153,"couplet":3,"v":["نگارم دوش در مجلس، به عزمِ رقص چون برخاست","گره بگشود از گیسو و بر دل‌های یاران زد"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[[27,30]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh153","en":"Last night in the gathering, when my beloved rose to dance,\nshe loosed a knot of her tresses and struck the hearts of her friends."},{"id":"ghazal/sh154#1","work":"ghazal","poem":154,"couplet":1,"v":["راهی بزن که آهی بر سازِ آن توان زد","شعری بخوان که با او رَطلِ گران توان زد"],"w":["ساز"],"hl":[[[19,23]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh154","en":"Play a tune on whose music one can heave a sigh;\nsing a verse with which one can drain a heavy cup."},{"id":"ghazal/sh158#5","work":"ghazal","poem":158,"couplet":5,"v":["من که شب‌ها رهِ تقوا زده‌ام با دف و چنگ","این زمان سر به ره آرَم؟ چه حکایت باشد! "],"w":["دف","چنگ"],"hl":[[[31,33],[36,39]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh158","en":"I who, night after night, have waylaid the road of piety with daf and harp—\nshall I now come to my senses? What a notion!"},{"id":"ghazal/sh163#3","work":"ghazal","poem":163,"couplet":3,"v":["رقصیدن سرو و حالتِ گُل","بی‌صوتِ هَزار خوش نباشد"],"w":["رقص","صوت"],"hl":[[[0,6]],[[3,7]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh163","en":"The dancing of the cypress and the mood of the rose—\nnot sweet without the voice of the nightingale."},{"id":"ghazal/sh164#8","work":"ghazal","poem":164,"couplet":8,"v":["مطربا مجلسِ انس است غزل خوان و سرود","چند گویی که چنین رفت و چنان خواهد شد؟"],"w":["سرود","مطرب"],"hl":[[[0,5],[31,35]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh164","en":"Minstrel, this is a gathering of intimacy: sing ghazal and song.\nHow long will you keep saying, “it went thus, and it will be thus”?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh165#4","work":"ghazal","poem":165,"couplet":4,"v":["خدا را محتسب ما را به فریادِ دَف و نِی بخش","که سازِ شرع از این افسانه بی‌قانون نخواهد شد"],"w":["دف","نی"],"hl":[[[29,32],[35,38]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh165","en":"For God's sake, censor, forgive us the cry of the daf and the ney,\nfor the instrument of the Law will not go out of tune over this tale.","note":"The wording plays on saz (instrument, also “order”) and qanun, which means “law” and is also the name of a zither-like instrument."},{"id":"ghazal/sh169#8","work":"ghazal","poem":169,"couplet":8,"v":["زهره سازی خوش نمی‌سازد، مگر عود‌ش بسوخت؟","کس ندارد ذوقِ مستی، مِی‌گسار‌ان را چه شد؟"],"w":["ساز"],"hl":[[[5,9]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh169","en":"Venus plays no sweet music now—can her lute have burned?\nNo one has a taste for drunkenness—what became of the wine-drinkers?","note":"‘Ud means the lute and also aloeswood, which is burned as incense; the question “has her ‘ud burned?” uses both senses."},{"id":"ghazal/sh173#8","work":"ghazal","poem":173,"couplet":8,"v":["مطرب از گفتهٔ حافظ غزلی نَغز بخوان","تا بگویم که ز عهدِ طربم یاد آمد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[0,4]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh173","en":"Minstrel, sing a fine ghazal of Hafez's words,\nthat I may say: the days of my gladness have come back to me."},{"id":"ghazal/sh174#2","work":"ghazal","poem":174,"couplet":2,"v":["برکش ای مرغِ سحر نغمهٔ داوودی باز","که سلیمانِ گل از بادِ هوا بازآمد"],"w":["نغمه"],"hl":[[[17,22]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh174","en":"Strike up again, bird of dawn, the song of David,\nfor the Solomon of the rose has come back on the wind."},{"id":"ghazal/sh178#9","work":"ghazal","poem":178,"couplet":9,"v":["داشتم دلقی و صد عیبِ مرا می‌پوشید","خرقه رهنِ مِی و مطرب شد و زُنّار بِمانْد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[],[[16,20]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh178","en":"I had a patched cloak that hid a hundred of my faults;\nthe cloak went in pledge for wine and the minstrel, and the infidel's girdle stayed.","note":"The zunnar is the cord worn by non-Muslims, a sign of unbelief."},{"id":"ghazal/sh179#5","work":"ghazal","poem":179,"couplet":5,"v":["سرودِ مجلسِ جمشید گفته‌اند این بود","که «جامِ باده بیاور که جم نخواهد ماند»"],"w":["سرود"],"hl":[[[0,5]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh179","en":"They say the song of Jamshid's gathering was this:\n“Bring the cup of wine, for Jam will not remain.”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh181#2","work":"ghazal","poem":181,"couplet":2,"v":["حاجتِ مطرب و مِی نیست تو بُرقَع بِگُشا","که به رقص آوَرَدَم آتشِ رویت چو سپند"],"w":["مطرب","رقص"],"hl":[[[6,10]],[[6,9]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh181","en":"No need of minstrel or wine—only lift your veil,\nfor the fire of your face has set me dancing like wild rue on the flame.","note":"Sepand is wild rue, whose seeds jump when thrown on fire."},{"id":"ghazal/sh184#5","work":"ghazal","poem":184,"couplet":5,"v":["شُکرِ ایزد که میانِ من و او صلح افتاد","صوفیان، رقص‌کنان، ساغرِ شکرانه زدند"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[],[[8,11]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh184","en":"Thanks be to God, peace has fallen between her and me;\nthe Sufis, dancing, raised the cup of thanksgiving."},{"id":"ghazal/sh185#6","work":"ghazal","poem":185,"couplet":6,"v":["رقص بر شعر تر و نالهٔ\nنی خوش باشد","خاصه، رقصی که در آن، دست نگاری گیرند"],"w":["رقص","نی"],"hl":[[[0,3],[22,24]],[[6,10]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh185","en":"Dancing to fresh verse and the lament of the ney is sweet,\nespecially a dance in which one takes a fair beloved's hand."},{"id":"ghazal/sh186#6","work":"ghazal","poem":186,"couplet":6,"v":["مطرب بساز پرده که کس بی‌اجل نمرد","وان کاو نه این ترانه سراید خطا کند"],"w":["مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[0,4],[10,14]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh186","en":"Minstrel, tune the mode, for no one ever died before his hour;\nand whoever does not sing this song is mistaken."},{"id":"ghazal/sh191#2","work":"ghazal","poem":191,"couplet":2,"v":["اول، بِه بانگِ نای و\nنی، آرد به دل، پیغام وی","وآن‌گه به یک پیمانه\nمی، با من وفاداری کند"],"w":["بانگ","نی"],"hl":[[[9,14],[15,18],[21,23]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh191","en":"First, with the sound of the pipe and the ney, let her send her message to my heart;\nthen, over one cup of wine, let her be faithful to me."},{"id":"ghazal/sh193#5","work":"ghazal","poem":193,"couplet":5,"v":["مفلسانیم و هوای می و\nمطرب داریم","آه اگر خرقهٔ پشمین به گرو نستانند!"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[21,25]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh193","en":"We are paupers, yet we long for wine and a minstrel—\nalas, if they will not take our woollen cloak in pledge!"},{"id":"ghazal/sh197#6","work":"ghazal","poem":197,"couplet":6,"v":["یارِ ما چون گیرد آغازِ سَماع","قُدسیان بر عرش دست‌افشان کنند"],"w":["سماع"],"hl":[[[23,28]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh197","en":"When our beloved begins the sama',\nthe holy ones on the Throne fling up their hands in dance."},{"id":"ghazal/sh200#1","work":"ghazal","poem":200,"couplet":1,"v":["دانی که چنگ و عود چه تَقریر می‌کنند؟","پنهان خورید باده که تَعزیر می‌کنند"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[8,11]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh200","en":"Do you know what the harp and the lute are declaring?\n“Drink your wine in secret, for they are meting out punishment.”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh202#5","work":"ghazal","poem":202,"couplet":5,"v":["گیسوی چنگ بِبُرّید به مرگِ مِیِ ناب","تا حریفان همه خون از مژه‌ها بگشایند"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[6,9]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh202","en":"Cut the tresses of the harp for the death of pure wine,\nthat the companions may all open their lashes to blood.","note":"Cutting the hair is a sign of mourning; the harp's strings are imagined as its tresses."},{"id":"ghazal/sh203#6","work":"ghazal","poem":203,"couplet":6,"v":["مُطرب از دَردِ محبت عملی می‌پرداخت","که حکیمانِ جهان را مژه خون پالا بود"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[0,5]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh203","en":"The minstrel, out of the pain of love, played a piece\nat which the sages of the world strained blood through their lashes.","note":"‘Amal can name a composed musical piece."},{"id":"ghazal/sh215#2","work":"ghazal","poem":215,"couplet":2,"v":["حدیثِ عشق که از حرف و صوت مُستَغنیست","به نالهٔ دف و نی در خروش و ولوله بود"],"w":["صوت","دف","نی"],"hl":[[[22,25]],[[9,11],[14,16]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh215","en":"The tale of love, which has no need of letter or sound,\nwas there in uproar and tumult with the lament of the daf and the ney."},{"id":"ghazal/sh219#2","work":"ghazal","poem":219,"couplet":2,"v":["بنوش جامِ صبوحی به نالهٔ دَف و چنگ","ببوس غَبغَب ساقی به نغمهٔ نی و عود"],"w":["دف","چنگ","نی","نغمه"],"hl":[[[25,28],[31,34]],[[20,25],[26,28]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh219","en":"Drink the morning cup to the lament of the daf and the harp;\nkiss the cupbearer's chin to the song of the ney and the lute."},{"id":"ghazal/sh219#3","work":"ghazal","poem":219,"couplet":3,"v":["به دورِ گُل منشین بی‌شراب و شاهد و چنگ","که همچو روزِ بقا هفته‌ای بُوَد معدود"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[35,38]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh219","en":"In the season of the rose do not sit without wine, a fair companion and the harp,\nfor like the span of life it is a week, soon counted."},{"id":"ghazal/sh219#7","work":"ghazal","poem":219,"couplet":7,"v":["چو گل سوار شَوَد بر هوا سلیمان‌وار","سحر که مرغ درآید به نغمهٔ داوود"],"w":["نغمه"],"hl":[[],[[20,25]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh219","en":"When the rose mounts the air like Solomon,\nat dawn, as the bird comes in with the song of David."},{"id":"ghazal/sh236#7","work":"ghazal","poem":236,"couplet":7,"v":["مانِعَش غلغلِ چنگ است و شکرخوابِ صَبوح","ور نه گر بشنود آهِ سحرم بازآید"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[14,17]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh236","en":"What holds her back is the clamor of the harp and the sweet sleep after the morning cup;\notherwise, if she heard my dawn sigh, she would come back."},{"id":"ghazal/sh238#4","work":"ghazal","poem":238,"couplet":4,"v":["نبود چنگ و رَباب و نَبید و عود، که بود","گِلِ وجودِ من آغشتهٔ گلاب و نَبید"],"w":["رباب","چنگ"],"hl":[[[5,8],[11,16]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh238","en":"There was no harp or rebab, no wine or lute yet,\nwhen the clay of my being was already steeped in rosewater and wine."},{"id":"ghazal/sh240#1","work":"ghazal","poem":240,"couplet":1,"v":["ابرِ آذاری برآمد بادِ نوروزی وزید","وَجهِ مِی می‌خواهم و مُطرب، که می‌گوید رسید؟"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[],[[21,26]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh240","en":"The March cloud has risen, the wind of Nowruz blows—\nI want money for wine and a minstrel: who will say “it has come”?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh241#2","work":"ghazal","poem":241,"couplet":2,"v":["به وقتِ سرخوشی از آه و ناله عُشّاق","به صوت و نغمهٔ چنگ و چَغانه یاد آرید"],"w":["صوت","نغمه","چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[3,6],[9,14],[15,18]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh241","en":"In your hour of merriment, remember the sighs and laments of lovers\nwith the voice and strain of the harp and the chaghana."},{"id":"ghazal/sh241#3","work":"ghazal","poem":241,"couplet":3,"v":["چو لطفِ باده کُنَد جلوه در رخِ ساقی","ز عاشقان به سرود و ترانه یاد آرید"],"w":["سرود"],"hl":[[],[[12,16]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh241","en":"When the grace of wine shows itself in the cupbearer's face,\nremember lovers with song and ballad."},{"id":"ghazal/sh243#10","work":"ghazal","poem":243,"couplet":10,"v":["ما مِی به بانگِ چنگ نه امروز می‌کشیم","بس دور شد که گنبدِ چرخ این صدا شنید"],"w":["بانگ","چنگ"],"hl":[[[10,15],[16,19]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh243","en":"It is not today that we drink to the sound of the harp;\nlong ago the dome of the heavens heard this noise."},{"id":"ghazal/sh244#3","work":"ghazal","poem":244,"couplet":3,"v":["رَباب و چنگ به بانگِ بلند می‌گویند","«که گوشِ هوش به پیغامِ اهلِ راز کنید»"],"w":["بانگ","رباب","چنگ"],"hl":[[[0,5],[8,11],[15,20]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh244","en":"Rebab and harp say, at the top of their voices:\n“Lend the ear of reason to the message of the people of the secret.”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh245#5","work":"ghazal","poem":245,"couplet":5,"v":["چه رَه بود این که زد در پرده مطرب؟","که می‌رقصند با هم مست و هشیار"],"w":["رقص","مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[24,28],[29,33]],[[6,11]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh245","en":"What way was this the minstrel struck within the mode?\nFor drunk and sober are dancing together.","note":"Rah (road) and pardeh (veil, fret) are both words for musical modes; the couplet plays on “road” and “mode”."},{"id":"ghazal/sh252#7","work":"ghazal","poem":252,"couplet":7,"v":["راز سربستهٔ ما بین که به دستان گفتند","هر زمان با دف و نی بر سرِ بازارِ دگر"],"w":["دف","نی"],"hl":[[],[[11,13],[16,18]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh252","en":"See our sealed secret, how they told it in tale and tune,\nwith daf and ney, each time in another bazaar.","note":"Dastan means a tale and also a tune."},{"id":"ghazal/sh254#1","work":"ghazal","poem":254,"couplet":1,"v":["دیگر ز شاخِ سروِ سَهی بلبلِ صبور","گلبانگ زد که چشمِ بد از رویِ گُل به دور"],"w":["بانگ"],"hl":[[],[[0,6]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh254","en":"Once more from the branch of the straight cypress the patient nightingale\nraised its rose-song: may the evil eye keep far from the rose's face."},{"id":"ghazal/sh254#6","work":"ghazal","poem":254,"couplet":6,"v":["مِی خور به بانگِ چنگ و مخور غصه ور کسی","گوید تو را که باده مخور گو هُوَالْغَفُور"],"w":["بانگ","چنگ"],"hl":[[[11,16],[17,20]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh254","en":"Drink to the sound of the harp and take no grief; and if anyone\nsays to you, “do not drink wine,” tell him, “God is Forgiving.”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh256#4","work":"ghazal","poem":256,"couplet":4,"v":["معاشری خوش و رودی بساز می‌خواهم","که دردِ خویش بگویم به نالهٔ بَم و زیر"],"w":["رود"],"hl":[[[13,17]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh256","en":"I long for a good companion and a well-tuned lute,\nthat I may tell my pain in laments, deep and high."},{"id":"ghazal/sh257#4","work":"ghazal","poem":257,"couplet":4,"v":["چنگ بِنْواز و بساز ار نَبُوَد عود چه باک؟","آتشم عشق و دلم عود و تَنَم مِجمَر گیر"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[0,3]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh257","en":"Play the harp and tune it—what matter if there is no aloeswood?\nTake love as my fire, my heart as the aloe, my body as the censer.","note":"‘Ud is both the lute and aloeswood (burned as incense); the couplet plays on both."},{"id":"ghazal/sh257#5","work":"ghazal","poem":257,"couplet":5,"v":["در سَماع آی و ز سر خرقه برانداز و برقص","ور نه با گوشه رو و خرقهٔ ما در سر گیر"],"w":["رقص","سماع"],"hl":[[[3,8],[34,38]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh257","en":"Come into the sama', throw the cloak from your head and dance;\notherwise go to your corner and put our cloak on your head."},{"id":"ghazal/sh258#9","work":"ghazal","poem":258,"couplet":9,"v":["غزل سُرایی ناهید صرفه‌ای نَبَرَد","در آن مَقام که حافظ برآورد آواز"],"w":["آواز"],"hl":[[],[[27,31]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh258","en":"Venus's ghazal-singing would gain no advantage\nin that station where Hafez raises his voice.","note":"Maqam means station and also musical mode. Nahid is Venus, the celestial musician."},{"id":"ghazal/sh259#7","work":"ghazal","poem":259,"couplet":7,"v":["فِکَنْد زمزمهٔ عشق در حجاز و عراق","نوایِ بانگِ غزل‌هایِ حافظ از شیراز"],"w":["بانگ"],"hl":[[],[[6,11]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh259","en":"It cast the murmur of love through Hijaz and Iraq—\nthe sound and call of Hafez's ghazals from Shiraz.","note":"Hijaz and Iraq are both places and names of musical modes."},{"id":"ghazal/sh262#6","work":"ghazal","poem":262,"couplet":6,"v":["بس که در پرده چنگ گفت سخن","بِبُرَش موی تا نَمویَد باز"],"w":["پرده","چنگ"],"hl":[[[9,13],[14,17]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh262","en":"So much has the harp said, behind the veil, in secret—\ncut off its hair, that it may not grow back.","note":"Pardeh means a veil and also a mode; a harp's strings are imagined as its hair."},{"id":"ghazal/sh267#4","work":"ghazal","poem":267,"couplet":4,"v":["من که قولِ ناصحان را خواندَمی قولِ رَباب","گوش‌مالی دیدم از هجران که اینم پند بس"],"w":["رباب"],"hl":[[[35,40]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh267","en":"I, who used to call the counsellors' words a mere tune on the rebab,\nhave had such a boxing of the ears from separation that this one lesson is enough.","note":"Qawl means a saying and also a song form."},{"id":"ghazal/sh275#2","work":"ghazal","poem":275,"couplet":2,"v":["طامات و شَطح در رَهِ آهنگِ چنگ نِه","تسبیح و طَیلَسان به مِی و مِیگُسار بخش"],"w":["آهنگ","چنگ"],"hl":[[[21,26],[27,30]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh275","en":"Lay your Sufi raptures and ecstatic claims down before the melody of the harp;\ngive your rosary and mantle to wine and the wine-drinker."},{"id":"ghazal/sh276#8","work":"ghazal","poem":276,"couplet":8,"v":["کیست حافظ تا ننوشد باده بی‌آوازِ رود؟","عاشقِ مسکین چرا چندین تجمل بایدش؟"],"w":["آواز","رود"],"hl":[[[27,32],[33,36]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh276","en":"Who is Hafez, that he should not drink wine without the sound of the lute?\nWhy should a poor lover need such splendor?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh278#3","work":"ghazal","poem":278,"couplet":3,"v":["بیاور مِی که نَتْوان شد ز مکرِ آسمان ایمن","به لَعبِ زهرهٔ چنگیّ و مرّیخِ سلحشورش"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[15,20]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh278","en":"Bring wine, for there is no being safe from the cunning of the sky,\nwith its harp-playing Venus at her game and its warrior Mars.","note":"Venus is the heavens' musician, here a harpist; Mars is the warrior planet."},{"id":"ghazal/sh283#3","work":"ghazal","poem":283,"couplet":3,"v":["به صوتِ چنگ بگوییم آن حکایت‌ها","که از نهفتنِ آن دیگِ سینه می‌زد جوش"],"w":["صوت","چنگ"],"hl":[[[3,7],[8,11]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh283","en":"To the sound of the harp let us tell those tales\nwhose concealment set the pot of the breast a-boil."},{"id":"ghazal/sh286#3","work":"ghazal","poem":286,"couplet":3,"v":["وان گَهَم دَر داد جامی کز فروغش بر فلک","زهره در رقص آمد و بَرْبَط زنان می‌گفت نوش"],"w":["بربط","رقص"],"hl":[[],[[8,11],[18,25]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh286","en":"Then she gave me a cup in whose radiance, up in the sky,\nVenus came dancing and, playing the lute, cried, “Drink!”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh286#4","work":"ghazal","poem":286,"couplet":4,"v":["با دلِ خونین لبِ خندان بیاور همچو جام","نی گَرَت زخمی رسد، آیی چو چنگ اندر خروش"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[26,29]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh286","en":"Keep a smiling lip over a bleeding heart, like the cup—\nnot, at one blow, to burst into wailing like the harp."},{"id":"ghazal/sh291#3","work":"ghazal","poem":291,"couplet":3,"v":["دوشم ز بلبلی چه خوش آمد که می‌سرود","گل گوش پهن کرده ز شاخِ درختِ خویش"],"w":["سرود"],"hl":[[[30,34]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh291","en":"Last night, how sweet it was, the nightingale that sang,\nwhile the rose, on its own branch, was all ears."},{"id":"ghazal/sh292#4","work":"ghazal","poem":292,"couplet":4,"v":["ببین که رقص‌کُنان می‌رود به نالهٔ چنگ","کسی که رُخصه نفرمودی اِسْتِماعِ سَماع"],"w":["رقص","سماع","چنگ"],"hl":[[[8,11],[34,37]],[[32,37]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh292","en":"See how he goes dancing to the lament of the harp,\nhe who gave no leave to listen to the sama'."},{"id":"ghazal/sh293#3","work":"ghazal","poem":293,"couplet":3,"v":["در زوایایِ طَرَبخانهٔ جمشیدِ فلک","اَرغَنون ساز کُنَد زهره به آهنگِ سَماع"],"w":["ساز","آهنگ","سماع"],"hl":[[],[[9,12],[27,32],[33,38]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh293","en":"In the corners of the heavens' pleasure-house of Jamshid,\nVenus tunes the arghanun to the strain of the sama'.","note":"The arghanun is an organ-like instrument; Venus is the musician of the heavens."},{"id":"ghazal/sh293#4","work":"ghazal","poem":293,"couplet":4,"v":["چنگ در غُلغُله آید که کجا شد منکر؟","جام در قَهقَهه آید که کجا شد مَنّاع؟"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[0,3]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh293","en":"The harp comes clamoring: “Where has the denier gone?”\nThe cup comes roaring with laughter: “Where is the forbidder?”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh296#6","work":"ghazal","poem":296,"couplet":6,"v":["من به خیالِ زاهدی، گوشه‌نشین و طُرفه آنک","مُغْبَچه‌ای ز هر طرف، می‌زندم به چنگ و دف"],"w":["دف","چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[33,36],[39,41]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh296","en":"I sit in a corner, fancying myself pious—and strangely,\nfrom every side some tavern lad plays at me with harp and daf."},{"id":"ghazal/sh304#6","work":"ghazal","poem":304,"couplet":6,"v":["شاها فلک از بزمِ تو در رقص و سَماع است","دستِ طَرَب از دامنِ این زمزمه مَگسِل"],"w":["رقص","سماع","طرب"],"hl":[[[23,26],[29,34]],[[5,10]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh304","en":"King, at your feast the heavens are in dance and sama';\nlet not the hand of joy let go the hem of this song."},{"id":"ghazal/sh309#2","work":"ghazal","poem":309,"couplet":2,"v":["ساقیِ شِکَّردهان و مُطربِ شیرین‌سخن","همنشینی نیک‌کردار و ندیمی نیک‌نام"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[19,25]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh309","en":"A sugar-mouthed cupbearer and a sweet-spoken minstrel,\na companion of good conduct and a boon friend of good name."},{"id":"ghazal/sh320#5","work":"ghazal","poem":320,"couplet":5,"v":["چشمم به رویِ ساقی و گوشم به قولِ چنگ","فالی به چشم و گوش در این باب می‌زدم"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[33,36]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh320","en":"My eye on the cupbearer's face, my ear on the word of the harp—\nin this matter I took an omen from eye and ear."},{"id":"ghazal/sh320#7","work":"ghazal","poem":320,"couplet":7,"v":["ساقی به صوتِ این غزلم کاسه می‌گرفت","می‌گفتم این سرود و مِیِ ناب می‌زدم"],"w":["صوت","سرود"],"hl":[[[8,12]],[[12,16]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh320","en":"The cupbearer held out the bowl to the sound of this ghazal of mine;\nI recited this song, and drank the pure wine."},{"id":"ghazal/sh324#3","work":"ghazal","poem":324,"couplet":3,"v":["پردهٔ مطربم از دست برون خواهد برد","آه اگر زان که در این پرده نباشد بارم"],"w":["مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[0,5],[6,11]],[[21,25]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh324","en":"The minstrel's mode will carry me out of my hands—\nalas, if I find no entry behind this veil.","note":"Pardeh means a mode and also a veil or curtain (the beloved's chamber); the couplet uses both."},{"id":"ghazal/sh332#7","work":"ghazal","poem":332,"couplet":7,"v":["مبادا جز حسابِ مُطرب و مِی","اگر نقشی کشد کِلکِ دبیرم"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[15,20]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh332","en":"May it be nothing but the account of minstrel and wine,\nif my scribe's pen draws any figure."},{"id":"ghazal/sh333#9","work":"ghazal","poem":333,"couplet":9,"v":["ز چَنگِ زهره شنیدم که صبح‌دم می‌گفت","«غلامِ حافظِ خوش‌لهجهٔ خوش‌آوازم»"],"w":["چنگ","آواز"],"hl":[[[2,7]],[[27,32]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh333","en":"I heard from Venus's harp, at dawn, the words:\n“I am the slave of Hafez, sweet of tongue and voice.”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh335#7","work":"ghazal","poem":335,"couplet":7,"v":["همچو چنگ ار به کناری ندهی کامِ دلم","از لبِ خویش چو نِی یک نفسی بِنْوازم"],"w":["چنگ","نی"],"hl":[[[5,8]],[[15,18]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh335","en":"If, like the harp, you grant my heart no desire in your embrace,\nthen from your own lips, like the ney, play me one breath.","note":"Kenar means a side and also an embrace; the harp is held in an embrace, the ney played with a breath from the lips."},{"id":"ghazal/sh336#4","work":"ghazal","poem":336,"couplet":4,"v":["بر سرِ تربتِ من با مِی و مُطرب بنشین","تا به بویت ز لحد رقص کُنان برخیزم"],"w":["رقص","مطرب"],"hl":[[[25,30]],[[17,20]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh336","en":"Sit by my grave with wine and a minstrel,\nthat at your scent I may rise dancing from the tomb."},{"id":"ghazal/sh340#9","work":"ghazal","poem":340,"couplet":9,"v":["گر از این دست زَنَد مُطربِ مجلس رَهِ عشق","شعرِ حافظ بِبَرَد وقتِ سماع از هوشم"],"w":["سماع","مطرب"],"hl":[[[20,26]],[[23,27]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh340","en":"If the minstrel of the gathering plays the road of love like this,\nHafez's verse at the hour of sama' will carry off my wits."},{"id":"ghazal/sh348#6","work":"ghazal","poem":348,"couplet":6,"v":["جرعهٔ جام بر این تختِ روان افشانم","غُلغُلِ چنگ در این گنبدِ مینا فکنم"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[8,11]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh348","en":"I will pour a drop from the cup upon this moving throne;\nI will cast the clamor of the harp into this enamel dome."},{"id":"ghazal/sh350#9","work":"ghazal","poem":350,"couplet":9,"v":["ز باده خوردن پنهان مَلول شد حافظ","به بانگِ بَربَط و نِی، رازَش آشکاره کنم"],"w":["بانگ","بربط","نی"],"hl":[[],[[3,8],[9,15],[18,21]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh350","en":"Hafez has grown weary of drinking wine in secret;\nto the sound of lute and ney I will make his secret plain."},{"id":"ghazal/sh351#2","work":"ghazal","poem":351,"couplet":2,"v":["مطرب کجاست تا همه محصولِ زهد و عِلم","در کارِ چنگ و بَربَط و آوازِ نِی کُنَم"],"w":["مطرب","چنگ","بربط","آواز","نی"],"hl":[[[0,4]],[[8,11],[14,20],[23,28],[29,32]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh351","en":"Where is the minstrel, that I may spend the whole harvest of my piety and learning\non the harp, the lute and the voice of the ney?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh359#7","work":"ghazal","poem":359,"couplet":7,"v":["به هواداری او ذَرِّه‌صفت، رقص‌کنان","تا لبِ چشمهٔ خورشیدِ درخشان بروم"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[[26,29]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh359","en":"In devotion to her, dancing like a mote,\nI will go to the very brim of the shining sun's spring."},{"id":"ghazal/sh360#3","work":"ghazal","poem":360,"couplet":3,"v":["تا بگویم که چه کشفم شد از این سیر و سلوک","به درِ صَومَعَه با بَربَط و پیمانه روم"],"w":["بربط"],"hl":[[],[[19,25]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh360","en":"So that I may tell what was disclosed to me by this journey on the Way,\nI will go to the door of the cloister with lute and cup."},{"id":"ghazal/sh367#5","work":"ghazal","poem":367,"couplet":5,"v":["بعد صد سال اگر بر سرِ خاکم گذری","سر برآرد ز گِلم رقص‌کنان عَظمِ رَمیم"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[],[[16,19]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh367","en":"If after a hundred years you pass by my grave,\nfrom my clay will rise, dancing, my rotted bones.","note":"“Rotted bones” echoes the Quran (36:78)."},{"id":"ghazal/sh372#6","work":"ghazal","poem":372,"couplet":6,"v":["چون صوفیان به حالت و رقصند مقتدا","ما نیز هم به شعبده دستی برآوریم"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[[21,26]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh372","en":"Since the Sufis, by ecstasy and dance, are made the leaders,\nwe too will lift a hand, with a conjurer's trick."},{"id":"ghazal/sh373#3","work":"ghazal","poem":373,"couplet":3,"v":["تا همه خلوتیان جام صبوحی گیرند","چنگ صبحی به در پیر مناجات بریم"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[0,3]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh373","en":"So that all the recluses may take the morning cup,\nlet us carry the morning harp to the door of the elder of prayer."},{"id":"ghazal/sh374#4","work":"ghazal","poem":374,"couplet":4,"v":["چو در دست است رودی خوش، بزن مطرب سرودی خوش","که دست‌افشان غزل خوانیم و پاکوبان سر اندازیم"],"w":["رود","سرود","مطرب"],"hl":[[[14,18],[28,32],[33,38]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh374","en":"Since a fine lute is at hand, minstrel, strike up a fine song,\nthat we may sing the ghazal with flung hands, and toss our heads as we stamp."},{"id":"ghazal/sh376#4","work":"ghazal","poem":376,"couplet":4,"v":["ارغنون ساز فلک ره‌زن اهل هنر است","چون از این غصه ننالیم و چرا نخروشیم؟"],"w":["ساز"],"hl":[[[7,10]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh376","en":"The heavens, that player of the organ, are a highwayman on the people of skill—\nhow should we not lament at this grief, why not cry out?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh376#6","work":"ghazal","poem":376,"couplet":6,"v":["می‌کشیم از قدح لاله شرابی موهوم","چشم بد دور که بی‌مطرب و مِی مدهوشیم"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[],[[17,21]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh376","en":"We drink an imagined wine from the tulip's cup—\nfar be the evil eye—we are entranced without minstrel or wine."},{"id":"ghazal/sh377#7","work":"ghazal","poem":377,"couplet":7,"v":["دلم از پرده بشد حافظ خوش‌گوی کجاست","تا به قول و غزلش ساز نوایی بکنیم"],"w":["ساز","پرده"],"hl":[[[7,11]],[[17,20]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh377","en":"My heart has slipped out of the veil—where is sweet-spoken Hafez,\nthat we may set a tune to his song and ghazal?","note":"Pardeh means a veil and also a mode; “out of the veil” suggests both a secret exposed and a voice gone out of its mode."},{"id":"ghazal/sh384#5","work":"ghazal","poem":384,"couplet":5,"v":["ای نورِ چشمِ مستان در عینِ انتظارم","چنگِ حزین و جامی بِنواز یا بگردان"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[0,4]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh384","en":"O light of the drunkards' eyes, I am in the very midst of waiting—\nplay the plaintive harp, or pass the cup around."},{"id":"ghazal/sh386#6","work":"ghazal","poem":386,"couplet":6,"v":["بیا وز غَبْن این سالوسیان بین","صُراحی خون‌دل و بربط خروشان"],"w":["بربط"],"hl":[[],[[16,20]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh386","en":"Come, and see, from the wrong of these hypocrites,\nthe flask a heart's blood, and the lute crying out."},{"id":"ghazal/sh391#7","work":"ghazal","poem":391,"couplet":7,"v":["بردم از ره دل حافظ به دف و چنگ و غزل","تا جزای من بدنام چه خواهد بودن"],"w":["دف","چنگ"],"hl":[[[22,24],[27,30]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh391","en":"I led Hafez's heart off the road with daf and harp and ghazal—\nwhat will be the reward of an ill-famed man like me?"},{"id":"ghazal/sh398#3","work":"ghazal","poem":398,"couplet":3,"v":["برگ نوا تبه شد و ساز طرب نماند","ای چنگ ناله برکش و ای دف خروش کن"],"w":["دف","ساز","طرب","چنگ"],"hl":[[[17,20],[21,24]],[[3,6],[22,24]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh398","en":"The provision of delight is ruined, and the instrument of mirth is gone;\nharp, raise your lament; daf, raise your cry."},{"id":"ghazal/sh413#8","work":"ghazal","poem":413,"couplet":8,"v":["حافظ که ساز مطرب عشاق ساز کرد","خالی مباد عرصهٔ این بزمگاه از او"],"w":["ساز","مطرب"],"hl":[[[8,11],[12,16],[22,25]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh413","en":"Hafez, who put the lovers' minstrel's instrument in tune—\nmay the field of this banquet never be empty of him."},{"id":"ghazal/sh415#1","work":"ghazal","poem":415,"couplet":1,"v":["ای پیک راستان خبر یار ما بگو","احوال گل به بلبل دستان‌سرا بگو"],"w":["دستان"],"hl":[[],[[17,22]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh415","en":"O messenger of the true, tell the news of our beloved;\ntell the rose's state to the song-singing nightingale.","note":"Dastan-sara: a singer of tales and tunes."},{"id":"ghazal/sh421#6","work":"ghazal","poem":421,"couplet":6,"v":["ز شور و عربدهٔ شاهدان شیرین‌کار","شکر شکسته، سمن ریخته، رباب زده"],"w":["رباب"],"hl":[[],[[22,26]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh421","en":"From the uproar and tumult of the sweet-working beauties:\nsugar broken, jasmine scattered, the rebab struck."},{"id":"ghazal/sh428#1","work":"ghazal","poem":428,"couplet":1,"v":["سحرگاهان، که مخمورِ شبانه","گرفتم باده با چنگ و چَغانه"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[14,17]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh428","en":"At dawn, hungover from the night,\nI took wine with harp and chaghana.","note":"Chaghana is a kind of musical instrument."},{"id":"ghazal/sh428#8","work":"ghazal","poem":428,"couplet":8,"v":["ندیم و مطرب و ساقی، همه اوست؛","خیالِ آب و گل در رَه، بهانه"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[7,11]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh428","en":"Companion, minstrel and cupbearer—all of it is He;\nthe fancy of water and clay along the road is only a pretext."},{"id":"ghazal/sh430#1","work":"ghazal","poem":430,"couplet":1,"v":["به صوتِ بلبل و قمری اگر ننوشی می","علاج کی کُنمت؟ آخِرالدَواءِ الْکَیْ"],"w":["صوت"],"hl":[[[3,7]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh430","en":"If you will not drink wine to the voice of the nightingale and the dove,\nhow shall I cure you? The last remedy is the cautery."},{"id":"ghazal/sh430#5","work":"ghazal","poem":430,"couplet":5,"v":["خزینه‌داری میراث‌خوارگان کفر است","به قولِ مطرب و ساقی، به فَتویِ دَف و نی"],"w":["دف","مطرب","نی"],"hl":[[],[[8,12],[31,34],[37,39]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh430","en":"Hoarding a treasury for those who will feast on your inheritance is infidelity—\nso say the minstrel and the cupbearer, so rules the fatwa of the daf and ney."},{"id":"ghazal/sh431#5","work":"ghazal","poem":431,"couplet":5,"v":["بزن در پرده چنگ ای ماه مطرب!","رگش بخراش تا بخروشم از وی"],"w":["مطرب","پرده","چنگ"],"hl":[[[7,11],[12,15],[23,27]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh431","en":"Strike the harp in its mode, O moon of minstrels,\nand scrape its string till I cry out because of it.","note":"Pardeh means a mode (or fret) and also a veil; the harp's strings are called its veins."},{"id":"ghazal/sh431#9","work":"ghazal","poem":431,"couplet":9,"v":["زبانت درکِش ای حافظ زمانی","حدیث بی‌زبانان بشنو از نی"],"w":["نی"],"hl":[[],[[23,25]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh431","en":"Hold your tongue a while, Hafez;\nhear the tale of the tongueless from the ney."},{"id":"ghazal/sh432#2","work":"ghazal","poem":432,"couplet":2,"v":["وصف رخ چو ماهش، در پرده راست نآید","مطرب بزن نوایی، ساقی بده شرابی"],"w":["مطرب","پرده"],"hl":[[[19,23]],[[0,4]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh432","en":"The praise of her moon-like face does not come out right in the veil;\nminstrel, strike up a tune; cupbearer, pour some wine.","note":"Pardeh means a veil (a veiled hint) and also a mode."},{"id":"ghazal/sh440#8","work":"ghazal","poem":440,"couplet":8,"v":["به شعر حافظِ شیراز می‌رقصند و می‌نازند","سیه‌چشمان کشمیری و تُرکان سمرقندی"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[[22,27]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh440","en":"To the verse of Hafez of Shiraz they dance and they strut—\nthe black-eyed beauties of Kashmir and the Turks of Samarkand."},{"id":"ghazal/sh442#8","work":"ghazal","poem":442,"couplet":8,"v":["ز پرده نالهٔ حافظ برون کی افتادی؟","اگر نه همدم مرغان صبح خوان بودی"],"w":["پرده"],"hl":[[[2,6]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh442","en":"How would Hafez's lament have slipped out of the veil,\nhad it not been the companion of the dawn-singing birds?","note":"Pardeh means a veil and also a mode; the lament slipping out of it suggests a secret exposed."},{"id":"ghazal/sh456#3","work":"ghazal","poem":456,"couplet":3,"v":["چنگ در پرده همین می‌دهدت پند ولی","وعظت آن گاه کند سود که قابل باشی"],"w":["چنگ","پرده"],"hl":[[[0,3],[7,11]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh456","en":"The harp, in its mode, gives you this very counsel; but\nthe sermon profits you only when you are fit to receive it.","note":"Pardeh means a mode and also a veil, a veiled hint."},{"id":"ghazal/sh460#3","work":"ghazal","poem":460,"couplet":3,"v":["خِرَد در زنده‌رود انداز و می نوش","به گلبانگ جوانان عراقی"],"w":["بانگ"],"hl":[[],[[3,9]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh460","en":"Throw reason into the Zayanda-rud and drink wine\nto the rose-song of the young men of Iraq.","note":"Zayanda-rud is the river of Isfahan; “Iraq” here is the Isfahan region (Iraq-e ‘Ajam)."},{"id":"ghazal/sh460#6","work":"ghazal","poem":460,"couplet":6,"v":["جوانی باز می‌آرد به یادم","سماع چنگ و دست افشان ساقی"],"w":["سماع","چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[0,4],[5,8]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh460","en":"Youth comes back to my mind:\nthe sama' of the harp and the cupbearer's flung hands."},{"id":"ghazal/sh460#11","work":"ghazal","poem":460,"couplet":11,"v":["بساز ای مطرب خوشخوان خوشگو","به شعر فارسی، صوت عراقی"],"w":["مطرب","صوت"],"hl":[[[8,12]],[[14,17]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh460","en":"Play, minstrel of the sweet voice and sweet speech,\nin Persian verse, the Iraqi strain.","note":"‘Iraqi’ names a musical mode and a region."},{"id":"ghazal/sh465#1","work":"ghazal","poem":465,"couplet":1,"v":["رفتم به باغ صبحدمی تا چنم گلی","آمد به گوش ناگهم آواز بلبلی"],"w":["آواز"],"hl":[[],[[17,21]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh465","en":"At daybreak I went into the garden to pick a rose;\nsuddenly the voice of a nightingale came to my ear."},{"id":"ghazal/sh465#5","work":"ghazal","poem":465,"couplet":5,"v":["چون کرد در دلم اثر آواز عندلیب","گشتم چنان که هیچ نماندم تحملی"],"w":["آواز"],"hl":[[[19,23]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh465","en":"When the nightingale's voice worked upon my heart,\nI became such that no endurance remained to me."},{"id":"ghazal/sh466#4","work":"ghazal","poem":466,"couplet":4,"v":["من حالت زاهد را با خلق نخواهم گفت","این قصه اگر گویم با چنگ و رباب اولی"],"w":["رباب","چنگ"],"hl":[[],[[20,23],[26,30]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh466","en":"I will not tell the ascetic's state to people;\nif I tell this tale, it is better told with harp and rebab."},{"id":"ghazal/sh474#3","work":"ghazal","poem":474,"couplet":3,"v":["بیفشان زلف و صوفی را به پابازی و رقص آور","که از هر رقعهٔ دلقش هزاران بت بیفشانی"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[[33,36]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh474","en":"Shake out your tresses and bring the Sufi to stamping and dance,\nthat from every patch of his frock you may shake out a thousand idols."},{"id":"ghazal/sh479#4","work":"ghazal","poem":479,"couplet":4,"v":["ساقی به دست باش که غم در کمین ماست","مطرب نگاه دار همین ره که می‌زنی"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[],[[0,4]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh479","en":"Cupbearer, be at hand, for grief lies in ambush for us;\nminstrel, hold to this very mode you are playing.","note":"Rah means a road and also a mode."},{"id":"ghazal/sh479#5","work":"ghazal","poem":479,"couplet":5,"v":["مِی ده که سر به گوش من آورد چنگ و گفت","«خوش بگذران و بشنو از این پیرِ منحنی»"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[28,31]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh479","en":"Pour wine, for the harp put its head to my ear and said:\n“Pass the time sweetly, and heed this bent old man.”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh479#6","work":"ghazal","poem":479,"couplet":6,"v":["ساقی به بی‌نیازی رندان که می بده","تا بشنوی ز صوت مغنی «هو الغنی»"],"w":["صوت"],"hl":[[],[[11,14]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh479","en":"Cupbearer, by the self-sufficiency of the rogues, pour the wine,\nthat you may hear from the singer's voice, “He is the Self-Sufficient.”"},{"id":"ghazal/sh486#1","work":"ghazal","poem":486,"couplet":1,"v":["بلبل، ز شاخِ سرو، به گلبانگِ پهلوی","می‌خوانْد دوش، درسِ مقاماتِ معنوی"],"w":["بانگ"],"hl":[[[21,28]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh486","en":"From the cypress branch, in a Pahlavi rose-song,\nthe nightingale last night was reciting the lesson of the spiritual stations.","note":"Maqamat are the stations of the spiritual path, and also musical modes; Pahlavi is Old Persian."},{"id":"ghazal/sh490#9","work":"ghazal","poem":490,"couplet":9,"v":["این حدیثم چه خوش آمد که سحرگه می‌گفت","بر درِ میکده‌ای، با دَف و نِی، ترسایی"],"w":["دف","نی"],"hl":[[],[[20,23],[26,29]]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh490","en":"How pleased I was with this saying, which at dawn\na Christian was singing at a tavern door, with daf and ney."},{"id":"ghazal/sh493#4","work":"ghazal","poem":493,"couplet":4,"v":["صَد بادِ صَبا، این‌جا، با سِلْسِلِه می‌رَقْصَنْد","این است حَریف ای دِل! تا باد نَپِیمایی"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[[39,48]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh493","en":"A hundred morning breezes dance here with the chain of her tress—\nthis is your adversary, heart, so do not go pacing the wind in vain."},{"id":"ghazal/sh495#8","work":"ghazal","poem":495,"couplet":8,"v":["هر مُرغ به دستانی در گلشنِ شاه آمد","بلبل به نواسازی، حافظ به غزل‌گویی"],"w":["دستان"],"hl":[[[11,17]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghazal/sh495","en":"Every bird has come to the king's rose garden with its own song—\nthe nightingale with melody-making, Hafez with ghazal-telling.","note":"Dastan means a tale and also a tune."},{"id":"ghete/sh9#4","work":"ghete","poem":9,"couplet":4,"v":["چون به هوای مدحتت زهره شود ترانه‌ساز","حاسدت از سماع آن محرم آه و ناله باد"],"w":["ساز","سماع"],"hl":[[[33,36]],[[9,13]]],"url":"/hafez/ghete/sh9","en":"When, in hope of praising you, Venus turns composer of songs,\nmay your envier, hearing it, be a companion of sighs and laments."},{"id":"ghete/sh26#4","work":"ghete","poem":26,"couplet":4,"v":["ساز چنگ، آهنگِ عشرت، صحن مجلس، جایِ رقص","خالِ جانان، دانهٔ دل، زلفِ ساقی، دام راه"],"w":["ساز","آهنگ","رقص","چنگ"],"hl":[[[0,3],[4,7],[9,14],[36,39]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghete/sh26","en":"The harp's playing, the tune of revelry, the courtyard of the gathering a place for dancing;\nthe beloved's mole the heart's grain, the cupbearer's curl the snare on the way."},{"id":"ghete/sh33#4","work":"ghete","poem":33,"couplet":4,"v":["بر مثانی و مثالث بنواز ای مطرب","وصف آن ماه که در حُسن ندارد ثانی"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[26,30]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghete/sh33","en":"Strike, minstrel, upon the second and third strings\nthe praise of that moon who has no second in beauty.","note":"Mathani and mathalith are lute-string terms (the second and third strings); the rhyme word thani, “second”, echoes them."},{"id":"robaee/sh39#1","work":"robaee","poem":39,"couplet":1,"v":["با شاهد شوخ شنگ و با بربط و نی","کنجی و فراغتی و یک شیشهٔ می"],"w":["بربط","نی"],"hl":[[[21,25],[28,30]],[]],"url":"/hafez/robaee2/sh39","en":"With a lively, charming beauty and with lute and ney,\na corner, some leisure and a flask of wine."},{"id":"ghaside/sh2#18","work":"ghaside","poem":2,"couplet":18,"v":["درون خلوت کروبیان عالم قدس","صریر کلک تو باشد سماع روحانی"],"w":["سماع"],"hl":[[],[[17,21]]],"url":"/hafez/ghaside/sh2","en":"Within the retreat of the cherubim of the sacred world,\nthe scratch of your pen is the spiritual sama'."},{"id":"ghaside/sh2#25","work":"ghaside","poem":2,"couplet":25,"v":["سحرگهم چه خوش آمد که بلبلی گلبانگ","به غنچه می‌زد و می‌گفت در سخنرانی"],"w":["بانگ"],"hl":[[[27,33]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghaside/sh2","en":"At dawn, how it pleased me that a nightingale was crying its rose-song\nto the bud, and saying in its speech:"},{"id":"ghaside/sh3#3","work":"ghaside","poem":3,"couplet":3,"v":["نوای چنگ بدان‌سان زند صلای صبوح","که پیر صومعه راه در مغان گیرد"],"w":["چنگ"],"hl":[[[5,8]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghaside/sh3","en":"The sound of the harp so calls to the morning cup\nthat even the cloister's elder takes the road to the Magi."},{"id":"ghaside/sh3#20","work":"ghaside","poem":3,"couplet":20,"v":["نوای مجلس ما را چو برکشد مطرب","گهی عراق زند گاهی اصفهان گیرد"],"w":["مطرب"],"hl":[[[25,29]],[]],"url":"/hafez/ghaside/sh3","en":"When the minstrel raises the music of our gathering,\nnow he plays Iraq, now he takes up Isfahan.","note":"Iraq and Isfahan are both places and names of musical modes."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#4","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":4,"v":["بده تا بگویم به آوازِ نی‌","که جمشید کی بود و کاووس کی"],"w":["آواز","نی"],"hl":[[[16,21],[22,24]],[]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Pour, that I may tell, to the voice of the ney,\nwhen Jamshid was, and when Kavus."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#31","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":31,"v":["که حافظ‌ چو مستانه سازد سرود‌","ز چرخَش دهد زُهره آوازِ رود‌"],"w":["سرود","آواز","رود"],"hl":[[[24,28]],[[18,23],[24,27]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"For when Hafez, drunk, makes his song,\nVenus, from her sphere, gives out the voice of the lute."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#32","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":32,"v":["مُغَنّی کجایی؟ به گلبانگِ رود","به یاد آور آن خسروانی‌سُرود‌"],"w":["بانگ","رود","سرود"],"hl":[[[18,25],[26,29]],[[22,27]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Minstrel, where are you? To the rose-call of the lute,\nbring to mind that royal song.","note":"Khosravani (“royal”) is also the name of an old musical mode."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#33","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":33,"v":["که تا وَجد را کارسازی کنم","به رقص آیَم و خرقه‌بازی کنم"],"w":["رقص"],"hl":[[],[[3,6]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"So that I may bring ecstasy to work,\nI will come into the dance and play the game of the cloak."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#43","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":43,"v":["مغنّی! بزن، آن نوآیین‌سرود‌","بگو با حریفان به آوازِ رود"],"w":["سرود","آواز","رود"],"hl":[[[22,26]],[[17,22],[23,26]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Minstrel, strike up that new-fashioned song\nand tell the companions, to the voice of the lute:"},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#45","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":45,"v":["مغنّی! نوایِ طرب ساز کن","به قول و غزل قصّه آغاز کن"],"w":["طرب"],"hl":[[[13,16]],[]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Minstrel, make the music of merriment;\nbegin the tale with song and ghazal."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#47","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":47,"v":["مغنّی! نوایی به گلبانگِ رود","بگوی و بزن خسروانی‌سرود"],"w":["بانگ","رود","سرود"],"hl":[[[16,23],[24,27]],[[19,23]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Minstrel, a melody to the rose-call of the lute—\nsing, and strike up the royal song."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#49","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":49,"v":["مغنّی! از آن پرده نقشی بیار","ببین تا چه گفت از درون، پرده‌دار"],"w":["پرده"],"hl":[[[13,17]],[[24,28]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Minstrel, bring a figure out of that veil;\nsee what the keeper of the curtain said from within.","note":"Pardeh means a veil and also a mode; naqsh means a figure and also a composed piece."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#50","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":50,"v":["چنان بَرکِش آوازِ خنیاگری","که ناهیدِ چَنگی به رقص آوری"],"w":["آواز","رقص","چنگ"],"hl":[[[12,17]],[[10,15],[19,22]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Raise the voice of the minstrel so high\nthat you set the harp-playing Venus dancing."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#52","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":52,"v":["مغنّی! دف و چنگ را ساز دِه","به آیینِ خوش‌، نغمه آواز دِه"],"w":["دف","ساز","نغمه","چنگ","آواز"],"hl":[[[7,9],[12,15],[19,22]],[[15,19],[20,24]]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"Minstrel, put the daf and the harp in tune;\nin the fine old way, give out the melody."},{"id":"saghiname/saghiname#58","work":"saghiname","poem":null,"couplet":58,"v":["به مستان، نویدِ سرودی فرست","به یارانِ رفته درودی فرست"],"w":["سرود"],"hl":[[[16,21]],[]],"url":"/hafez/saghiname","en":"To the drunkards send the glad tidings of a song;\nto the friends who have gone send a greeting."}]};
